# Staged payload checkout (GOALS.md G6.3/G6.1, `grid.py checkout`). The
# committed home of these bytes is the node's own grid ref — this directory is
# a working copy of it in exactly the sense git's worktree is a working copy of
# the index, so losing it costs nothing and committing it would be the second
# copy the whole design exists to avoid.
.agi/payloads/

# Generated by the loop. nodes/ IS committed — the nodes are the thoughts.
.agi/sessions/
# The declared season-level comms root (<graph_root>/comms/season-<N>/) is
# graph content and MUST stay tracked — the room/dm files are the council
# record, not scratch (hypothesis:l3-send-comms-root). Do not extend the
# sessions/ ignore above to .agi/comms/.
.agi/context/INJECTION.md
# Written by publish-engine.sh on every run, read by metrics.py
# (hours_since_successful_publish) and hooks/cc-session-start.sh (goal:g7.10).
# Machine state about this checkout, not graph content, so it is generated like
# INJECTION.md rather than committed. It is also why the marker does not live
# under nodes/: gate 0 refuses on any uncommitted change there, so a marker
# written into the graph would arm, on every run, the gate it exists to report.
.agi/context/publish-state.json
.agi/nodes.db
# dashboard.py writes this to `<nodes_dir>/.chain_cache.pkl`, i.e. inside the
# graph directory itself — not beside it. unify.py's migration map assumed
# `.agi/.chain_cache.pkl` and the rule was one directory off, so a binary cache
# sat untracked in committed graph content and every kid reported it.
.agi/.chain_cache.pkl
.agi/nodes/.chain_cache.pkl
.agi/loop.log

# Agent worktrees + local caches
.agi/worktrees/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# pi harness run log, written into the graph dir by a kid (goal:s28 session)
.agi/autoresearch.jsonl
# ...and the SAME artifact at the repo root, which the pi runtime actually writes.
# The rule above was one directory off: payload_boundary.py:97 already names this
# exact gap ("autoresearch.jsonl at repo root does not [live under a gitignored
# directory], despite being the same kind of artifact") and excludes it from being
# minted as a payload -- but nothing stopped git from tracking it. It was retired
# from this repo on 2026-09-06 (99082b2ab) and every pi round re-creates and stages
# it; git history is the archive, not a to-do list to keep re-adding to.
/autoresearch.jsonl
# Read-cursor sidecars beside room/dm files are per-reader state, not the record.
.agi/comms/**/*.state.json

# stray budget/session dir written by the L3.25 git_common_root helper (hypothesis:l3-budget-dir-dropped-agi) — never commit; the real dir is .agi/sessions/
sessions/

# .env backups (key rotation) — hold FULL live credentials, never commit
.env.bak*
.env.old*
.env.save*

# rotation records are the durable evidence of a rotation; committed, unlike
# the transient session logs beside them. Git cannot re-include a path under
# an ignored dir, so un-ignore .agi/sessions/ and re-ignore every child EXCEPT
# rotations/ and quorum/ (future transients land under .agi/sessions/* and
# stay ignored). quorum/ holds per-seat successor briefs -- load-bearing for
# rotation, not scratch, and a force-add every generation has to remember is
# a manual step outside the system that silently stops happening the first
# time someone forgets it (2026-09-08, belam, against sanctuary-director
# gen II's own force-add of this same file minutes earlier).
!.agi/sessions/
.agi/sessions/*
!.agi/sessions/sensei/
!.agi/sessions/rotations/
!.agi/sessions/rotations/*
!.agi/sessions/quorum/
!.agi/sessions/quorum/*
!.agi/sessions/handoff-sections/
!.agi/sessions/handoff-sections/*

# repo-root scratch a kid's own measurement tooling lands in (e.g. a throwaway
# venv for tiktoken) -- disposable, never a work product; see .agi/tmp/ for
# the durable equivalent inside a worktree.
/tmp/
